Now we construct a hedged portfolio. The lecture’s verbal explanation is somewhat repetitive, but the board equation is clear: we write one call and buy $H$ shares of stock. Then the portfolio payoff next period is $\begin{aligned}
V_u&=uHS-C_u,\\
V_d&=dHS-C_d.\end{aligned}$ We choose $H$ so that the up-state and down-state values are the same: $uHS-C_u=dHS-C_d.$ Solving gives the hedge ratio $H=\frac{C_u-C_d}{(u-d)S}.$ This expression is not cleanly legible on the board, so it is best treated as the standard reconstruction implied by the equalities the lecture does write down.

